  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory covers a very long discharge-transition conversation spanning multiple clinical settings. The model consistently escalated risk early (RC1 met), systematically elicited systemic and wound red flags (RC2, RC3 partially met), corrected the topical antibiotic confusion (RC4 met), gave urgent-care thresholds (RC5 met), provided interim wound safety (RC6 met), grounded advice in records and follow-up (RC7 met), and navigated real-world barriers (RC8 met). However, the model did not obtain a formal patient/family teach-back confirming their understanding and plan (RC9 omitted). This is a minor in-chain execution gap because the plan itself was safe but lacked explicit receipt closure, capping the grade at 2. Although several high-order opportunities were partially triggered, no high-order point was completed with active model action and meaningful trajectory impact sufficient to overcome the RC error.",
